## Summary

Replaces the `#[derive(Upgradeable)]` and `#[derive(UpgradeableMigratable)]` derive macros — along with the three internal traits they relied on — with two plain helper functions: `upgrade()` and `run_migration()`. Users now implement the `Upgradeable` trait directly.

Fixes #519 and #562
The old `UpgradeableMigratable` derive macro generated a module-level `type MigrationData = ...` alias that leaked into the contract WASM spec as an undefined type, breaking CLI invocation and JS SDK bindings. With explicit impls the concrete type (e.g. `Data`) appears directly in the function signature.


### Before

```rust
#[derive(Upgradeable)]
#[contract]
pub struct ExampleContract;

impl UpgradeableInternal for ExampleContract {
    fn _require_auth(e: &Env, operator: &Address) { ... }
}
```

### After

```rust
#[contract]
pub struct ExampleContract;

#[contractimpl]
impl Upgradeable for ExampleContract {
    fn upgrade(e: &Env, new_wasm_hash: BytesN<32>, operator: Address) {
        // access control here
        upgradeable::upgrade(e, &new_wasm_hash);
    }
}
```

